@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Managing Environments in Azure DevOps";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to effectively manage environments in Azure DevOps for efficient deployment and testing.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What are Environments in Azure DevOps?</h2>
        <p>
            In Azure DevOps, an <strong>Environment</strong> is a logical grouping of resources that can be used for deployment and testing.
            It provides a way to define and control the infrastructure and application lifecycle across different stages.
        </p>
        <p>
            Environments support Kubernetes clusters, virtual machines, and other Azure services, ensuring a structured approach to managing deployments.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/environments-overview.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Environments Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Environments enable controlled deployment stages and testing.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Setting Up Environments -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Setting Up Environments in Azure DevOps</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Go to your Azure DevOps project and navigate to <strong>Pipelines &rarr; Environments</strong>.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click on <strong>New Environment</strong> and give it a meaningful name.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Choose the resource type (Kubernetes, Virtual Machine, or other Azure resources).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Define deployment triggers and approval gates if required.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Save the environment and integrate it with your pipeline.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/setup-environment.jpg" alt="Setting Up Environments" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Creating an environment in Azure DevOps.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Managing Deployments -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Managing Deployments Across Environments</h2>
        <p>Best practices for managing deployments across environments include:</p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Approval Gates:</strong> Set up pre-deployment and post-deployment approvals.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automate Testing:</strong> Run automated tests before moving to production.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Variables and Secrets:</strong> Store environment-specific configurations securely.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor Deployments:</strong> Track logs and performance metrics for insights.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Rollback Strategy:</strong> Define a rollback mechanism in case of failures.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/deployment-management.jpg" alt="Managing Deployments in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Effective deployment strategies ensure stability and reliability.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Managing environments in Azure DevOps is crucial for ensuring a smooth deployment pipeline. By setting up structured environments,
            implementing approval workflows, and monitoring deployments, organizations can achieve continuous delivery with confidence.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/conclusion.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Environments Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Environments help streamline deployments and improve software quality.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>